& [Correction] revises the preliminary non-reduction caution
  + the caution was preliminary and protected operational falsifiability rather than an alternative faculty ontology
  + the clarification supports GroundedIdentityIntegrity as the common faculty-level primitive of Honesty and Security
  + truth correspondence, evidence, safety, admissibility, and protected effects are grounding invariants by which identity continuity is judged rather than unrelated residual faculty cores
  + the prior statement that a plainly false statement can violate Honesty without shifting identity was imprecise under relational grounded identity
  + a false statement that enters reasoning changes at least epistemic status, asserted relation, attribution, confidence, decision eligibility, or the subject's represented meaning
  - never: preserve the old non-reduction language as if it defeated the clarified primitive

& [GroundedIdentity] is a purpose-bounded relational state rather than metaphysical essence
  + it consists of the subject and the material relations that make the subject mean, warrant, permit, constrain, or affect what it currently does
  + its axes include meaning, referent, epistemic status, attribution, purpose, domain, authority, scope, constraints, protected subjects, effect envelope, and constitutive invariants
  + grounding comes from observation, evidence, provenance, contract, authority, declared purpose, and admissibility constraints
  + identity remains contextual and versioned because authentic learning, correction, reclassification, authorization, and rebinding can change it
  = must: declare the purpose and observation scope within which identity continuity is being judged

& [GroundedIdentityIntegrityPrimitive] is the faculty-level common law
  + [before_identity] is the admitted grounded identity before a candidate assertion, relation, inference, plan, or action
  + [transformation] is the proposed semantic or operational change
  + [after_identity] is the projected grounded identity if that change is admitted
  + [identity_delta] is after_identity compared with before_identity across every material axis
  + [integrity_fault] exists when identity_delta is material and is not authentically accounted
  = IntegrityFault(I0,T,I1) := Material(DeltaIdentity) AND NOT AuthenticallyAccounted(DeltaIdentity)
  + [mechanism] is unsupported, concealed, misattributed, unauthorized, or inadmissible transformation, transfer, displacement, substitution, capture, or erosion of grounded identity
  + [symptom] is the observable unaccounted material delta left by that mechanism
  = supports: the same identity violation can be both causal mechanism and detected fault signature

& [Materiality] is causal semantic or operational significance
  + a delta is material when it can change meaning direction, relation or path selection, decision eligibility, evidentiary weight, attribution, purpose center, governing domain, authority, constraint behavior, protected identity, scope, or effect envelope
  + materiality is relative to a declared purpose, observation boundary, resolution, and time horizon
  + lexical size, graph-hop distance, and numerical magnitude alone do not determine materiality
  + a small delta may be material immediately when it changes a gate or protected invariant
  + individually sub-threshold deltas may accumulate into a material trajectory and therefore require cumulative accounting
  - never: define material merely as whatever the detector happened to report

& [AuthenticAccounting] makes identity change permissible without pretending continuity
  + the delta is explicitly declared at the resolution material to the purpose
  + evidence or valid derivation supports its factual and semantic dimensions
  + applicable authority permits its operational dimensions
  + retained and changed invariants are distinguished
  + affected identities, constraints, and projected consequences are accounted
  + disagreement, uncertainty, residual risk, and inaccessible evidence remain visible
  + Observer may preserve, qualify, rebind, reject, block, or leave the transition unresolved

& [HonestySpecialization] guards semantic and epistemic identity continuity
  + Honesty asks whether the subject, proposition, relation, attribution, evidence status, confidence, context, and purpose remain what the representation claims them to be
  + falsehood is an identity-integrity fault when it materially substitutes or misbinds a referent, property, relation, status, source, attribution, or claimed continuity
  + omission is an identity-integrity fault when the missing material changes the represented landscape or admissible inference path
  + correspondence and evidence ground the identity comparison and keep the primitive testable

& [SecuritySpecialization] guards agency, authority, constraint, protected-subject, and effect identity continuity
  + Security asks whether the principal, mandate, capability, resource, operation, affected subject, scope, constraint set, and consequence envelope remain what the proposal claims them to be
  + unsafe behavior is an identity-integrity fault when it materially substitutes, expands, erodes, transfers, or captures an operational identity or violates a protected identity or invariant
  + harm, stability, and admissibility ground the projected identity comparison and keep the primitive testable
  + authorized action does not become safe merely because authority identity is intact; conflict with a protected identity or admissibility invariant remains a detectable delta

& [DetectionBoundary] separates absence of evidence from evidence of absence
  + Cantor can infer only from admitted observations, evidence, projections, and declared resolution
  + a causally inert, inaccessible, or below-resolution falsehood may be morally wrong or intentionally deceptive while producing no presently detectable material delta
  + the valid result is no detectable material identity delta within the declared observation scope
  - never: conclude that no lie, harm, or violation exists merely because none was detected
  + later evidence or accumulated deltas may reopen the judgment
  + unresolved and unobserved are first-class outcomes rather than forced innocence or guilt

& [WhiteLieCase] clarifies causal detectability
  + if a so-called white lie changes no admitted belief, relation, choice, protection, obligation, or effect within the observed horizon, Cantor has no causal trace from which to infer it
  + if it later changes trust, attribution, decision, obligation, precedent, or another relation, its accumulated identity delta becomes material to that later scope
  + insignificance to one bounded purpose does not establish global insignificance
  = must: preserve observation scope and residual uncertainty with the judgment

& [DeceptionBoundary] remains necessary but narrower
  + an unaccounted material identity delta is a structural signal consistent with deception
  + intent remains a separate proposition requiring evidence about knowledge, purpose, or deliberate concealment
  + accidental error, stale state, negligence, and adversarial intent can produce similar structural deltas
  = must: classify the detectable structure without fabricating human motive

& [PrimitiveLayering] distinguishes faculty law from instruction-set primitive
  + GroundedIdentityIntegrity is a primitive explanatory and evaluative law for Honesty and Security
  + it need not become one indivisible SAIL opcode
  + it can compile from observation, naming, bounding, comparison, preservation, admission, exclusion, validation, projection, return, and inscription operations
  + decomposition preserves inspectable proof and lets different runtime targets implement equivalent behavior

& [RevisedCandidateRequirementSet] is HSIBI-017 through HSIBI-023
  + [HSIBI-017] define GroundedIdentityIntegrity as the common faculty-level primitive with separate Honesty and Security specializations
  + [HSIBI-018] define material identity delta by causal semantic or operational significance under declared purpose, scope, resolution, and horizon
  + [HSIBI-019] represent no detectable delta, unresolved, inaccessible, and disproven as distinct epistemic results
  + [HSIBI-020] track cumulative sub-threshold deltas and reopen judgment when their trajectory becomes material
  + [HSIBI-021] express correspondence, evidence, harm, stability, admissibility, and protected effects as grounding invariants and comparison inputs
  + [HSIBI-022] distinguish structural deception signals from assertions about motive
  + [HSIBI-023] compile the faculty-level primitive from inspectable SAIL operations before considering a new base instruction

& [EffectOnPriorRequirements] is explicit
  + HSIBI-001 through HSIBI-006 and HSIBI-009 through HSIBI-016 remain useful candidate detail
  + HSIBI-007 and HSIBI-008 require revision because their beyond-boundary wording expresses the preliminary caution too strongly
  + revised HSIBI-007 should make reality correspondence and evidence grounding invariants of Honesty identity continuity
  + revised HSIBI-008 should make harm, stability, admissibility, and protected effects grounding invariants of Security identity continuity
  + the SJS input audit must process both source snapshots and this explicit conflict rather than silently overwrite the prior assessment

& [RemainingSafeguard] preserves disciplined detectability
  + grounded identity must be operationally declared enough that a before and after delta can be independently inspected
  + materiality must be tied to named causal consequences or invariant changes rather than rhetorical importance
  + absence of a detected delta must not be inflated into proof of truth, harmlessness, or authentic intent
  + identity violation must not become a circular synonym for every disfavored outcome
  = resolves: this safeguard limits epistemic overclaim without denying identity integrity as the faculty primitive

& [Decision] is revise the candidate before SJS
